      "narrative": "The copper lamp above your table flickers as Mara Venn leans back, her charcoal coat creaking. She takes a slow drag from a cigarette, smoke curling around her sharp features, and fixes you with those hawk-bright eyes.\n\n\"The Ash Gate.\" She lets the words hang. \"Old Bram used to work the lock. Knew it like the back of his hand. Swore by the Kestrel Guild's seal \u2014 said it'd hold a hundred years.\"\n\nShe taps ash onto the scarred tabletop.\n\n\"Then they found him facedown in the mud three weeks ago. Heart gave out, they said. Convenient, that.\"\n\nHer gaze drifts toward the shuttered window, and you catch something flicker behind her eyes \u2014 a thread of knowing, a half-glimpsed shape just out of reach. She *almost* says something. Her lips part.\n\nThen Toran Vex clears his throat from the next table, ink-stained fingers drumming against a ledger. Mara's jaw tightens. The moment passes.\n\nShe stubs out her cigarette.\n\n\"That's all I've got, ranger. Bram's dead. Gate's sealed. The Guild's not talking.\" She meets your gaze flatly. \"What's your interest in a locked door, anyway?\""
    },
