      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyebrow cocks at your question. She reaches for another cigarette, then thinks better of it, her fingers settling on the table instead.\n\n\"Maintained the lock?\" She lets out a dry chuckle. \"That'd be Toran.\"\n\nThe clerk at the next table looks up sharply, his ink-stained fingers freezing mid-drum.\n\nMara gestures at him with a lazy thumb. \"Toran Vex was the Guild's lockkeeper before they sealed the Gate. Knew every pin, every ward, every trick that old mechanism had. Bram just worked the ferry \u2014 Toran kept the lock *working*.\"\n\nShe watches your face for a reaction, then adds, almost idly:\n\n\"Of course, that was before the Guild went quiet. Before they stopped answering questions. Before they told Toran his services were no longer required.\"\n\nToran Vex shifts uncomfortably, his eyes darting between you and Mara. He's holding a ledger against his chest like a shield.\n\nMara leans forward, voice dropping.\n\n\"Ask him yourself. He's right there.\" She tips her chin toward the nervous clerk. \"If he'll talk.\""
    },
