      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyes narrow at the insistence in your voice. She holds your gaze for a long moment \u2014 measuring, weighing something behind those sharp irises. Then she reaches into her coat and pulls out a crumpled scrap of parchment, sliding it across the scarred table.\n\n\"Name's Sable Quill.\"\n\nShe taps the parchment. On it, in a hurried hand, is scrawled: *Sable Quill \u2014 courier \u2014 last seen at the Gate.*\n\n\"Sold passage for three seasons. Had a deal with Bram \u2014 he worked the ferry, she worked the *customers*. Took coin, arranged crossings, kept the Guild's cut.\" Mara's voice drops lower. \"When Bram turned up dead and the Guild sealed the lock, she vanished. No one's seen her since.\"\n\nShe leans back, letting you study the scrap.\n\n\"Last I heard, she was still holed up near the Gate somewhere. Waiting, maybe. Or hiding.\""
    },
