      "narrative": "The name echoes off the cracked stone of the arch and fades into the grey distance. No answer comes from the gate itself \u2014 only the hollow whisper of wind threading through the iron bars, a sound like a held breath slowly released.\n\nBut then \u2014 there.\n\nTo your left, a flicker of motion in the shadow of a collapsed wall, half-swallowed by morning haze. The faintest rustle of fabric, the scrape of a boot sole on stone. Someone is there, pressed against the dark, watching you.\n\nAnd as your eyes track the movement, you notice something else. The snagged fabric scrap at the base of the gate \u2014 that frayed dark cloth \u2014 *shivers*. Vibrates, faintly, as if something on the other side of the iron bars is pulling at it from behind."
    },
