      "narrative": "The walk back feels shorter than the journey out. The street rises beneath your boots, the shuttered buildings of the lower quarter giving way to the familiar shape of the Copper Finch's rain-dark facade. Smoke curls from its chimney, thin and grey against the overcast sky.\n\nThe door groans as you push it open. Warmth hits you \u2014 the hearth fire, the smell of old ale and beeswax, the low murmur of a handful of patrons keeping to themselves. A few heads turn, register you, look away.\n\nYour table stands where you left it. The scarred wood, the faint ring stains from countless mugs, the chair that sits slightly crooked on uneven floorboards. Mara Venn is nowhere in sight \u2014 perhaps in the back, perhaps gone. Toran Vex's usual corner is empty.\n\nThe tavern settles back into its quiet rhythm around you. The fire pops. A spoon clinks against a bowl somewhere. Through the window, the Ash Gate is just a dark speck at the end of the sloping street.\n\nThe scrap of fabric from the gate is still in your hand. You hadn't realized you were still holding it."
